WEBVTT

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.540
"MELTY Popularity Ranking"

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.540
"5th Reo Igarashi"

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.870
Reo!

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:56.700
Next time... I promise to make you number one!

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.700
So...

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.120
Okay.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.660
Cham's event schedule has been updated!

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.040
Hey, there's a sports festival!

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.870
"I Promise to Make You Number 1"
Yay! I love events like this!

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.500
The important part is below that.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.450
Below?

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.000
"25th Reo Igarashi's Birthday Concert"

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.910
Reo's birthday. 'Grats.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.080
You have absolutely no interest, do you?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.580
That's important, too, but below that!

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.040
Yeah, whatever.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.700
"Popularity Ranking Voting"
"Results will be announced at the end of November"
"We look forward to your support. (1 CD will equal 1 vote)"

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.660
No!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.660
I was waiting for this day to come,
and it's finally arrived!

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.950
Is there some kind of punishment for whoever's last?

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.290
You're giving up way too fast!

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.160
How are the handshake lines looking right now?

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.160
Reo's in the clear lead.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.830
I know that.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.120
Next up is Sorane, and then Maki,
who has a little less.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.370
Yuka has about the same.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.660
And then...

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.410
Probably Yumeri?
And then A-ya, and then Maina.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.410
So the voting ends at the end of November...

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.500
Even people who don't usually
buy duplicates will go all out for this.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.750
I'm gonna need the 30,000 Maina fans around Japan
to step up their game so Maina can be the center.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.500
Wow, really? You're actually thinking that
right now? Did you hit your head?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.790
There could be plenty that
just never leave their houses!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.830
Oh, I know your secret.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:02.580
I know that you go to Maina's blog and post
numerous comments under various names--

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.950
Don't ever say that again.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.660
Ever.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.580
No!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.790
You really don't have to worry about it that much.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.540
It's not like everyone other than first place
has to graduate or anything.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.620
But...

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.580
If you work really hard,
you might even get to be the center!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.000
I'm gonna work super hard!

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.540
I'm totally fine where I am.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.870
It sounds like a lot of work being in the top 3.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.450
You're actually somewhat popular,
so you have room to say that!

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.830
I don't want this...

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:42.950
If Yuka works really hard,
Maki might get knocked out of the top 3!

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.950
Or rather...

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.910
What if my own fans work really hard for me...

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.080
And then...

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.250
"Yumeri Mizumori"

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.700
Let's both be in the show next year.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.540
I promised Maki. So what am I...

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.250
You'll be fine, Yume.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.700
Your fans know how hard you're working.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:16.700
Maki...

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.580
No, that's not it.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.620
Yeah, I'm not a huge fan either

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.200
when they try to rank us like this.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.700
Reo.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.080
But you see...

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.040
You have fans.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.330
Okay?

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.910
What's with all of you?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.250
You all look like the sheath on
the Momotaro statue broke again.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.250
"Autumn Sports Festival"

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.700
We've got this to worry about
before the popularity ranking.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.700
"Autumn Sports Festival"
That's right...

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.620
Huh... I guess we're renting out
a gym from a grade school this year.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.950
Well, there was a certain girl
who tried way too hard

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.830
in the tiny studio last year
and broke both of her legs.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.870
Is something wrong, Maina?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.950
I wish I was like you, Sorane.
I'm terrible at sports.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.950
Well, Sorane-<i>chin </i>does play tennis.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.660
Tennis, huh?

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.160
She plays tennis, so we don't stand a chance.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.120
What do all of you even think tennis is?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.750
"Autumn Sports Festival"
"Entrance"
ChamJam's...

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.660
...Autumn Sports Festival!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.830
"Autumn Sports Festival"

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.700
Sorane, A-ya, and Yumeri are on the red team.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.500
Maki, Yuka, and Maina are on the white team.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.540
And your ref will be me, Reo!

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.660
I hope you cheer the girls on!

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.040
Do your best out there, Reo!

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.250
Our ref better not break her legs!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.000
I won't!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.790
So she's the ref...

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.250
Can you blame her? The poor girl
broke both of her legs last year.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.290
It must be traumatic.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.580
Wait, why did they even make a photo of this?

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.750
This was a secret draw!

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:18.790
I'm sure that Motoi feels rather defeated
right now since he's at home with a cold.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.620
A <i>wota </i>who can't properly take care
of himself must pay the consequences.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:28.580
Our first event is the team relay!

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.580
Start!

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.370
Wait...

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.540
Was A-ya always that fast?!

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.040
A-ya. Just look at you go. You're amazing!

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.620
You're cute and sporty!

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.580
I'll just have to vote for you.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.500
I guess I'll have to change my fave.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.000
First! First! First!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.660
A-ya!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.700
Aya-<i>chin</i>, you okay?

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.700
Come on!

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.540
Th-This little...

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.200
She helped A-ya out
even though she's on the other team!

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:14.830
Yuka's so sweet!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.620
Guess I'll have to vote for her.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.620
Guess I'll have to change my fave.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.290
I know exactly what you're up to, you moron!

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.540
What?!

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.910
But Yumeri's such a good dancer...

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.830
I guess that doesn't matter.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.910
It's like they're both taking a nice stroll.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.910
Maina! You've got this!

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.250
Eripiyo!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.540
Huh?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.250
Yumeri!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.750
I have to run... For my fans!

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.830
Sorane's really fast,

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:05.580
so if I just hand off the baton to her,
Maki won't be able to win.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.580
Maki!

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.160
You did good, Maina.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.950
Wow, look at Sorane go!

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.370
She's leaving Maki in the dust!

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.540
And she crossed the finish line!

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.040
"Sorane"
The red team wins!

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.910
Sorane!

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:40.200
You ran so good, Maina! I'm so moved!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.830
Yume. We need to both do our best.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.450
Wait, is this about the sports festival?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.500
That, too, but...

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:52.910
...also the ranking.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.620
But I...

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:03.200
Then how about the loser has to do
whatever the winner says?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.950
That'll motivate you, right?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.120
Yeah.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.000
Let's both do our best, okay?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Come on, get up, A-ya.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.080
Can't. I give up.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.540
We're still on our first event.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:25.450
We're switching refs!

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.000
I'm going to join the red team!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.580
Don't break your legs again!

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.330
I won't!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.540
But if I do, I'm sorry.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:36.790
Reo!

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:38.040
Break a leg!

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.040
Break three!

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.080
Uh, should you guys get that excited about that?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.040
There!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.250
--Take that!
--There!

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.410
There!

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:51.410
Ow!

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.450
"Bread-eating Contest"

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.830
"Scavenger Hunt"

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.580
U-Um...

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.290
A-A <i>kokeshi </i>doll?

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:13.120
Maina! Here!

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.290
"Tug-o-war"

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.370
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:26.750
Oh, hey. Wouldn't the team with the most
overall weight have an advantage?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:27.750
Heave...

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.290
"Ball Rolling"

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.410
And I'm back!

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.290
And now for the results!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.500
The white team got 45 points.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.870
And the red team... 68 points!

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.450
"Winner: Red Team"
The red team wins!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.750
I didn't break my legs!

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.290
Reo!

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.580
I'm so glad I got to take
an event photo op with you.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.040
Thank you!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.660
I'm even happier that you
didn't get hurt this year.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.250
Say, Kumasa...

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:16.330
That time when you said you'd
make me number 1 next time...

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:20.950
...and then that group broke up
and there never was a next time...

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.950
But...

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:29.160
Next time... I promise to make you number one!

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.040
So...

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.580
Believe in me.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:38.120
Is it okay for me to keep believing in you?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.040
Of course!

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.870
I can finally keep my promise.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.120
Great job, Maina!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.450
You look ultra-cute in your gym outfit!

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.870
What a coincidence! We match!

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:02.200
I-It's a little embarrassing...

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:07.700
Hey, for the popularity ranking...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.700
Huh?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.750
Nothing will make me happier
than you taking first place.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.160
So I'll vote for you as many times as I can.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.290
You have fans.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.000
So try believing in them.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.660
Upsy-daisy.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.000
Eripiyo.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.330
Thank you...

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:32.410
...for everything that you do.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.410
Sure!

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:41.080
I'll believe in Eripiyo, who always
works so hard for me.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.660
And I need to do whatever it takes
to take first place!

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.040
"I updated my blog #MakiHakata"
"Thanks for all your support at the sports festival.
Make sure you get plenty of rest tonight."

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:50.750
"I updated my blog #YumeriMizumori"
"Thanks to everyone who participated in the sports festival.
It was so much fun..."

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:51.790
"I updated my blog #AyaYokota"
"I'm cosplaying Reo."

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.870
They're all so good at updating their blogs.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.950
"I updated my blog #MainaIchii"
"Oh, my goodness! <i>Tsukudani </i>was only 50 yen!"
And Maina's posting her usual...

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:05.540
"Popularity rankings can be rough,
but I'll do my best!"

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:13.830
Maina...

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.660
I'm so proud of you for saying that.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:20.000
I'm going to leave 80 comments today!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.540
With different names, of course.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.200
Her birthday's not fair!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.790
And by that you mean...?

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.040
The place is going to be filled with Reo stans!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:36.500
Can we just make Maina's birthday next week?!

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:40.870
More importantly, apparently,
there's no saving your taste.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:44.830
I've never met a girl <i>wota</i>
who lacked this much talent.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.500
Well, I've never done this before.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.370
Cham just started letting us celebrate
their birthdays with them this year.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.950
You keep complaining even though
I'm trying to help you out,

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.080
so what are you doing?

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.500
I'm ordering the cake and flower stand.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.370
Oh, and the glowsticks.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:06.830
Hey, isn't this going to get harder every year?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:11.540
I mean, who knows when the last birthday
we'll celebrate will be?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.950
Put that death flag down!

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.370
I gathered some more message cards.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:17.870
Sorry to put you to work
as soon as you were better.

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:22.500
That's fine. But why ask me
rather than other Reo stans?

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.200
Well, I'm in charge of the birthday committee,

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.620
but that's about all they want from me.

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:34.250
They became even more distant
after the Halloween concert last year.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.750
Yeah...

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.830
That reminds me, it's coming up very soon!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.410
What are you going to cosplay this year?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.410
I'm not cosplaying this year!

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:45.160
I swear to God,
I'm not doing that again! I want friends!

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:48.200
You won't leave us, will you, Motoi?

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.790
Huh? Uh, sure.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.540
But to be honest,
the more I hang out with these two,

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.660
the more I stand out, too.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.580
Might be time to call it off soon.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.080
By the way, how much are you paying me an hour?

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.000
I'm not!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.200
Just thought I'd ask.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.830
But in the end, I really am broke.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:09.330
All <i>otaku </i>are broke.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:12.500
"Please vote for us"
That's right. We're all flat broke.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.250
She's so fast! But the belt's
not moving any faster!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.290
Can you even see, Eri?

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.160
Thank you!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.830
So that's how it works. You got it?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:37.080
Perfectly! I'm an expert at flipping over bread!

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.750
And there's absolutely no need
for you to flip over bread here.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.160
Thank you!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.540
Why does she look like she's flipping over bread?

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.790
Thank you...

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.200
Whoa, Eripiyo!

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.450
Huh?

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.870
Oh, sorry.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.290
Are you all right? You don't look too well.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:14.500
I don't... I don't have any money!

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.700
Also, if I'm going to spend money
at a family restaurant,

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.450
I'd rather buy more of Maina's CDs.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.790
Er, I'm paying our tab here.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.830
Why not take some time off from work?

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.200
Don't worry!

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.910
It'd be even harder for me if Maina was last.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:33.790
Here's this week's pay.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.080
Thank you very much!

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.660
That's worth 30 CDs!

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.250
Here you go. Great job.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:41.870
That's worth 26 CDs!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.540
Here you go. Thanks.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.120
That's worth 24 CDs!

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:54.500
Okay... Tomorrow's Reo's birthday celebration.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.910
I'm going to give my all into voting for Maina.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:07.040
"Reo Igarashi Birthday LIVE"
Thanks for everything you did as
the birthday committee lead, Kumasa.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.160
Congrats to Reo.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.580
Thank you very much.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.450
Eripiyo...

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:15.830
Hey!

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:17.330
She's gravely injured again!

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.410
Wait, what happened?!

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.410
Well...

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.620
Oink!

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:31.700
It appears that wildlife attacks are finally
an issue even in Okayama City.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.950
No, no, no! You need to go home and rest!

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.830
Being a part-timer's just not gonna cut it.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:42.660
I'd probably be better off financially
if I worked in an office.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:46.040
Office employees can't get days off easily.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.200
And that's exactly why I quit my office job.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.540
Wow, you're trash, Kumasa.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.950
I'll give up on job-hunting, too.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:55.200
You're both trash...

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.290
"Glow Sticks"
Upsy-daisy.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:19:00.200
Well, I'm going to go hand out the glowsticks.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.950
Yeah! Let's do this!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.000
"Today is Reo's birthday. Please use your
glowsticks during Reo's solo song after the talk
segment. Please keep these hidden until then."

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:16.410
Kumasa.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.370
I got you a place up front.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:23.620
I got a pretty low line number,
so I saved you a spot.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:24.540
Come on.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.330
But I...

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.700
Get over here, Kumasa!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:29.910
--Yeah.
--Yeah.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.200
Please.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.540
Kumasa! Come on!

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.410
Thank you, everyone.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:03.410
♪ I get lonely easily and
need you to dote on me ♪

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.500
♪ Even then, I'm somehow the oldest! ♪

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:09.080
The leader in pink, Reo!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.120
Dear Reo Igarashi, happy birthday.

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:29.200
Thank you for always supporting
the rest of us as our leader.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.790
Looking back, you and I--

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:40.250
To the other girls, and to our fans...

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.660
Thank you so much for today!

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.080
"Happy Birthday, Reo Igarashi!!"
"From your fans"

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.750
Yeah, this was a great birthday party.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.000
Not to mention, Maina was as cute as ever today.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:12.290
I mean... It's going to take me
a month to recover, but...

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.000
"Maina CDs 1000 yen"
But... That's not important right now!

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.660
I'd like 80 of Maina's CDs!

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.040
You're kidding!

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:24.080
"Popularity Ranking Results
1st Reo, 2nd Sorane, 3rd Maina, 4th Maki,
5th Yuka, 6th Yumeri, 7th Aya"

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.540
"Popularity Ranking Results
1st Reo, 2nd Sorane, 3rd Maina, 4th Maki,
5th Yuka, 6th Yumeri, 7th Aya"
Last place...?

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.830
I'm last place?!

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:30.450
It'll be okay. I'm 6th--

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.000
But you're above me!

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.450
Dang, Maina-<i>chin</i>. You're in 3rd place!

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:38.120
Good for you, Maina.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.040
Wait, am I in trouble?

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.500
Hey, Maina.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:48.080
Aren't you glad you believed in your fans?

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.660
Yeah!

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.370
Thank you, Eripiyo.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.500
"Halloween Concert"
"Doors 17:00" "Show 18:00"
Maina did great!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:59.790
Well, all 30,000 Maina fans
across Japan did their best.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:05.000
But I won't be able to work for a while.
Doctor's orders.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:07.580
I'm worried what'll happen without my votes...

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:09.540
I'm so nervous I'm gonna puke...

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.870
Eripiyo...

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:12.870
By the way...

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.790
...is it just me, or are we standing out?

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:18.200
"The Truth"

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:19.790
"Last Halloween"

00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:22.450
Two top <i>wota</i>s are both cosplaying!

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:26.040
I see! We're supposed to cosplay, too!

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:31.330
Crap...

00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:34.370
Now people are going to think
I'm actually close to these two again.

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:07.500
"Next episode preview"
Breaking news, A-ya!

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:10.620
I figured this day would come someday,
but it's finally here, A-ya!

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:12.790
ChamJam's popularity ranking!

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:15.620
Apparently, Eripiyo changed her fave. Right, A-ya?

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:16.500
--But...
--You know...

00:24:16.500 --> 00:24:18.660
You're the only one for us, A-ya!

00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:20.040
"I Can Only Wait"
Thank you very much!
